AI System Design Interviews : How to Approach 


The 7-Step Framework --

This framework is a structured methodology designed to guide teams through the development of robust, scalable, and maintainable AI systems—from initial concept to production deployment and beyond. It breaks down the system design and production engineering lifecycle into seven manageable steps, ensuring that every aspect of the process is addressed methodically.

1. Define Objectives and Scope
Purpose: Clearly articulate the problem you are solving and the business or technical objectives of your AI system.
Key Actions:
Identify primary use cases and target users.
Specify success criteria and measurable KPIs.
Establish constraints (e.g., latency, throughput, scalability).
2. Gather and Analyze Requirements
Purpose: Dive into detailed requirements, both functional and non-functional, to understand what the system must deliver.
Key Actions:
Engage stakeholders to collect user and technical requirements.
Assess performance, security, and compliance necessities.
Document requirements and create a clear specification document.
3. Architect and Design the System
Purpose: Develop a high-level system design ensuring modularity, scalability, and robustness.
Key Actions:
Design the overall architecture, including data flow, component interactions, and integration points.
Choose appropriate AI models, databases, microservices, and APIs.
Create data models, interface designs, and error handling strategies.
4. Prototype and Validate Concepts
Purpose: Build a proof-of-concept (POC) to test key assumptions and verify design choices early in the cycle.
Key Actions:
Develop prototypes or low-fidelity versions of critical system components.
Validate the feasibility of AI algorithms on sample data.
Collect user feedback and refine requirements.
5. Implement and Integrate
Purpose: Transition from design to development by building and integrating all system modules based on established architecture.
Key Actions:
Follow iterative development cycles, implementing features in modules.
Use CI/CD pipelines to integrate new code and automate testing.
Ensure rigorous code reviews and adhere to best practices for maintainability and performance.
6. Test, Deploy, and Monitor
Purpose: Validate system performance and reliability before releasing into production; then continuously oversee system operation.
Key Actions:
Execute comprehensive testing (unit, integration, load, and security tests).
Deploy using containerization, orchestration, or cloud platforms ensuring scalability.
Set up monitoring tools to track performance, logs, and system health; prepare for incident management.
7. Maintain and Optimize
Purpose: Continuously improve the system post-deployment through monitoring, feedback, and iterative enhancements.
Key Actions:
Perform regular maintenance, back-ups, and updates.
Analyze user feedback and system performance metrics to identify optimization opportunities.
Plan for scaling, refactoring, and incorporation of emerging AI techniques.
