Explain that fallback chains are a vital part of building fault-tolerant systems.
Discuss potential scenarios where advanced patterns (such as circuit breakers combined with fallback chains) are appropriate.
Be prepared to talk about real-world examples, like service failovers and degenerated modes of operation.
